 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+These properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` record the measured semantics that hook features specify against. The `onError` boundary remains out of scope; issue #93 defines the aggregate usage delivered after tool rounds.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the summed provider-call usage for the entire turn, so tool rounds are included in a deployer's billing or audit total ([validated by: reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
+- Rounds that report no usage do not reduce the total; a turn where some rounds lack usage still accumulates the totals from rounds that do report, while a turn where no round reports usage delivers `undefined` to the hook ([validated by: counts reported rounds while leaving a turn with no reported usage undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+- When no round in a turn has reported usage, the accumulated total stays `undefined` ([validated by: returns undefined when both accumulator and round are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L11)).
+- The first round to report usage seeds the total; before any round has reported, there is no accumulator ([validated by: returns the round usage when accumulator is not yet set](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L15)).
+- A round that reports no usage leaves the total unchanged ([validated by: returns the accumulator unchanged when the round reports no usage](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L20)).
+- When both the accumulated total and the current round carry usage, all three token fields are summed ([validated by: sums all three token fields when both accumulator and round report usage](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L25)).
+- The round loop continues only when the stop reason is `tool_use`, the model named at least one tool, and a registry is configured; it stops if any condition fails ([validated by: continues when the model requested a tool and a registry can run it](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L33)).
+- With no registry configured the loop does not continue regardless of what the model asked for ([validated by: stops when no registry is configured, whatever the model asked for](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L37)).
+- With no tool calls pending the loop does not continue even when the stop reason is `tool_use` ([validated by: stops when the model named no tool](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L41)).
+- With a stop reason other than `tool_use` the loop does not continue regardless of pending calls ([validated by: stops when the model finished for a reason other than tool use](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L45)).
